# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code local settings (machine-specific permission grants)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Obsidian workspace state (per-machine UI state, not vault content)
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Plugin config with a live API key (marker-api's mistralaiApiKey) -- never commit
.obsidian/plugins/marker-api/data.json

# stray / editor / OS
.trash/
*.lnk
wf_test_after.log

# Third-party Obsidian plugin code, not vault content
.obsidian/plugins/

# Reproducibility caches: out/ accumulates one directory per tier/run and is
# regenerated by the scripts in scripts/, not hand-authored. Ignored by
# default; the current case study's artifacts are force-included below since
# the wiki cites them directly.
out/*
!out/w93/
out/w93/*
!out/w93/w93.json
!out/w93/w93.pre-w98.json
!out/w93/frames.json
!out/w93/state.npz
!out/w93/wake-array.html
!out/w93/wake-array-template.html
# CS-9 (thermal strain): 14 KB, cited line by line by
# case-study-thermal-strain-atlas-0.1.md and read back by tests/test_tier23.
!out/w94/
out/w94/*
!out/w94/w94.json
# PoC 1a, frozen-expert column: 3 MB, cited line by line by
# poc1a-frozen-expert-results.md and merged from the per-stage artifacts under
# the same directory (those stay ignored -- only the merged record is kept).
!out/w118/
out/w118/*
!out/w118/w118.json
# CS-9* (seam placement): the search record and the horizon march, cited line
# by line by tier0-measurements.md §21 and case-study-seam-placement-atlas-0.1.md
# and re-derived cold by tests/test_tier25_seam_placement.py. w112.json is 4.5 MB.
!out/w112/
out/w112/*
!out/w112/w112.json
!out/w112/horizon.json
# CS-10 (ground effect): the moving-interface record -- the L(h) curve, the six
# marches, the operator drift, W97's three efforts, the gradient's horizon sweep
# and the four compiles -- cited line by line by
# case-study-ground-effect-atlas-0.1.md and re-derived by
# tests/test_tier27_ground_effect.py.  130 KB.
!out/w127/
out/w127/*
!out/w127/w127.json
# CS-11 (brake thermal): the multirate record -- the sigma-vs-interval law and
# the bound evaluated against it, the clock-ratio control, the waveform sweep,
# the accumulated march and the gradient's horizon table -- cited line by line
# by case-study-brake-thermal-atlas-0.1.md and re-derived by
# tests/test_tier28_brake_thermal.py.  The run log beside it stays ignored.
!out/w131/
out/w131/*
!out/w131/w131.json
# CS-12 (wing FSI): the FSI record -- the structural surface operator, the four
# compiles and W114's control, the seam's three efforts and its blindness, the
# gate's tip histories, R across the seam, the added-mass map and the gradient's
# horizon table -- cited line by line by case-study-wing-fsi-atlas-0.1.md and
# re-derived by tests/test_tier29_wing_fsi.py.  The settled-field cache beside it
# (settled.npz, 470 KB of float64 velocity) stays ignored: it is regenerated in
# 25 s by `--stages setup` and nothing cites it.
!out/w136/
out/w136/*
!out/w136/w136.json

# PoC 2 (the front-wing assembly): the assembly's two limit controls, the
# per-seam verdict maps, the thickness scaling the design box is drawn from,
# both degrees of freedom's gate histories, R across both seams, the four-knob
# horizon table, the cost measurement, the finite-difference step sweep, the
# penalty sweep, the ablation at BOTH the reference design and the optimum, and
# FOUR design runs -- `design` (the answer), `design_tight` (the ceiling placed
# where it binds inside the envelope), `design_unenforced` (W145's evidence: the
# same search with no envelope check on the objective's path) and `design_loose`
# (the first, loose-ceiling box search).  All four are kept because a ceiling
# moved until the answer is agreeable is not a constraint, and the only defence
# is to keep every placement with its outcome.  Cited line by line by
# poc2-frontwing-results.md and re-derived by tests/test_tier30_front_wing.py.
# The settled-field cache beside it (settled.npz) stays ignored: it is
# regenerated in 4 s by `--stages setup`, bit-identically, and nothing cites it.
!out/w141/
out/w141/*
!out/w141/w141.json

# Tier 32 (control observability): gate 0's twelve reference-trace rows with the
# full J(s) line behind each, gate 1's spectra at three probe states for four
# agents -- every singular value, not just beta_ctrl and kappa -- the null
# direction's overlap with the constant modes, the DtN blocks read off the same
# marches, the sigma triple (lagged / perfect-seam-datum / solved) with all three
# regularisation sweeps, and the five instrument controls including the epsilon
# sweep that breaks at Poseidon-T's declared floor.  Cited line by line by
# control-observability.md and re-derived by
# tests/test_tier32_control_observability.py, which skips rather than fails
# without it.  The run is reproducible from cold and was verified bit-identical
# leaf by leaf, so the file is a convenience and not the only copy.
!out/w149/
out/w149/*
!out/w149/w149.json

# Tier 33 (the interaction horizon): gate A's fourteen configurations with Pi,
# the measured Pi_w, both implied constants and the recorded-sigma reproduction
# beside each; gate B's influence profiles at three probe states for five agent
# columns -- the full seventy-shell profile in max AND mean, the far-field
# spectrum with its effective rank and the constant-mode overlap, and the
# per-mode decay table that splits the two families; gate C's Poseidon-T
# horizon; the whole-graph Pi_w with and without the one-scalar pin; and the
# Tier 32 confound read back from out/w149.  Cited line by line by
# interaction-horizon.md and re-derived by
# tests/test_tier33_interaction_horizon.py, which skips rather than fails
# without it.  Reproducible from cold and verified bit-identical leaf by leaf.
!out/w153/
out/w153/*
!out/w153/w153.json

# Tier 35 (W159, the cut defect bound on the front-wing graph): 128 KB, the
# chi-weighted bound and both reference-free surrogates at every one of 160
# exchanges across two columns, with the composed defect and the evaluated
# identity residual beside each -- plus the zero-cut control's own 80 rows,
# which are the reason to keep the per-exchange detail rather than the summary.
# Cited line by line by gap-worklist Tier 35 and by log.md.  Reproducible from
# cold: scripts/w159_frontwing_cut_defect.py, deterministic, repeat floor
# measured at exactly 0.
!out/w159/
out/w159/*
!out/w159/w159.json

# Tier 38 (W166, the neural interface predictor): 38 KB, and it is the whole
# record of a NEGATIVE, which is the reason to keep it rather than a summary.
# Five predictor arms in two arrangements with their skills, sweep counts and
# solve costs; the eleven-row halo sweep in both arrangements, which is where
# the as-built contraction is seen crossing 1 between halo 18 and halo 20; the
# four-accelerator ladder at three tolerances with the probe's own kappa,
# alpha_star and rho(D^-1 S) beside it; and both compiles.  Cited line by line
# by case-study-neural-interface-atlas-0.1.md, gap-worklist Tier 38 and log.md.
# Reproducible from cold: scripts/w166_neural_interface.py; every part but the
# Poseidon arm is deterministic and needs no torch (--no-neural).
!out/w166/
out/w166/*
!out/w166/w166.json

# Tier 40 (W173 the epsilon-halo, W174 the refusal validation, W177 the
# campaign census, W171 the decomposition scope). JSON only: w173's
# seam_operators.npz is 1.2 MB of dense operators and is a rebuildable cache.
!out/w173/
out/w173/*
!out/w173/w173.json
!out/w173/transverse.json
!out/w174/
out/w174/*
!out/w174/w174.json
!out/w177/
out/w177/*
!out/w177/w177.json
!out/w171/
out/w171/*
!out/w171/w171.json

# Tier 41 (CS-S2 the bounded donor, W137's visibility check). JSON only:
# cs_s2's operators.npz holds dense operators measured on third-party weights
# that are kept OUTSIDE this repository (~/.cache/neubernet, no licence), and
# it is a rebuildable cache.
!out/cs_s2/
out/cs_s2/*
!out/cs_s2/cs_s2.json
# the hoop-sign diagnosis, both conventions side by side; the second run's
# artifact it corrects stays local (cs_s2_run2_hoop_plus1.json)
!out/cs_s2/torsion_control.json
!out/cs_s2/sign_jump.json
!out/w137/
out/w137/*
!out/w137/w137.json
# Tier 42 (W181/W182, the inequality-seam probe). JSON only, and it is small:
# the whole artifact is three compiles, one nine-decade sweep and two censuses
# over declarations. Committed because tests/test_tier42_inequality_seam.py
# asserts the page's figures against it rather than retyping them, and because
# the run is six seconds of numpy from cold -- no checkpoint, no torch, no
# network -- so a fresh clone can rebuild it or check it, either way.
!out/w181/
out/w181/*
!out/w181/w181.json
# Tier 43 (rung 3, CS-17: the learned pair). JSON only. The dense operators are
# not written at all here -- the artifact carries the spectra, the block norms
# and every decision message, which is what the page quotes and the tests
# assert. NeuberNet is UNLICENSED and local-only, so nothing derived from its
# weights beyond measured numbers is committed, and no test loads it.
!out/rung3/
out/rung3/*
!out/rung3/rung3.json
# Tier 44 (W171 part 1, the per-region decomposition axis). JSON only, and
# small: the control over every constructible case graph, the union graph's
# two-axis report, and the before/after rule coverage the page quotes and the
# tests assert. `before.json` is the same run with the three rules unchanged --
# kept because the finding is a DIFFERENCE and half of it is not reproducible
# from this tree any more.
!out/w171b/
out/w171b/*
!out/w171b/w171b.json
!out/w171b/before.json
# Tier 45 (W189, the partition of unity, overlap and overlap cells per region).
# JSON only. The byte-identity control is committed as MANIFESTS -- one sha256 per
# graph for all forty constructible case graphs, before the change (twice, under
# two PYTHONHASHSEEDs, which is the repeat floor) and after it -- together with
# the two comparisons tests/test_tier45_region_assembly.py asserts, the partition
# census the per-region shape was chosen on, and the union measurement the page
# quotes. The full artifacts behind the hashes (artifacts/, ~5 MB) and the run
# logs stay local: they are rebuilt by scripts/w189_artifact_control.py, and the
# hashes are what the test compares.
!out/w189/
out/w189/*
!out/w189/control_before1.json
!out/w189/control_before2.json
!out/w189/control_after.json
!out/w189/compare_before1_vs_before2.json
!out/w189/compare_before1_vs_after.json
!out/w189/census.json
!out/w189/w189.json
# Tier 49: W194 is a behaviour change, so the byte-identical control was
# re-run against it. 38 of 40 artifacts identical, 2 differ (both Tier 44
# union fixtures, multirate by agents with no multirate seam), 0 uncompared.
# tests/test_tier45_region_assembly.py asserts the pair and the count.
!out/w189/control_tier49.json
!out/w189/compare_before1_vs_tier49.json
# Tier 46 (W172, the joining seams and the O(K) count across them). JSON only:
# the one record scripts/w172_joining_cost.py writes -- the counter control, the
# fourteen unions, each join's marginal cost at two family counts, both insertion
# orders, the four rotor-port forms, the clocks, the physics controls and the
# device-down passivity control on wake_array's own graph.
# tests/test_tier46_joining_seams.py asserts against it.
!out/w172/
out/w172/*
!out/w172/w172.json
# Tier 47 (W198, rung 9's gate restated). JSON only: the record
# scripts/rung9_gate.py writes -- N on the vehicle graph, what R(t) needs against
# what the records declare, each join's receiving balance with and without its
# term, the rotor's power path and a host-sized rotor's operating point, and the
# coolant loop's response to the air. tests/test_tier47_rung9_gate.py asserts
# against it.
!out/rung9/
out/rung9/*
!out/rung9/rung9.json
# Tier 48 (W202 onward, what a learned expert can contribute: the kill tests and
# defect correction). JSON only: the record scripts/w202_kill_tests.py writes --
# the reproduction control, the per-call costs, the classical settled state's
# residual and error histories, the warm starts, every defect-correction arm, the
# energy certificate's floor, self-consistency and the fine-tuning price.
# tests/test_tier48_learned_contribution.py asserts against it. The .npz caches
# hold the classical settled states -- 26 MB, and the reference stage rebuilds
# them (19 s at two windows, 244 s at six, longer at twelve), so they are
# ignored rather than committed.
!out/w202/
out/w202/*
!out/w202/w202.json
# Tier 50 (W205, the corruption sweep). JSON only: the record
# scripts/w205_corruption_sweep.py writes -- the reproduction control against
# Tier 48's own cell, the magnitude x direction grid of defect-correction arms,
# the per-magnitude summary and its pre-registered verdict, and the derivative
# probe (per-band Rayleigh quotients for every map, Theorem 2's assembled
# eigenvalues, and the rank correlations against classical calls).
# tests/test_tier50_corruption_sweep.py asserts against it.
#
# **Rebuilding it is not seconds.** The six-window grid is twelve directions at
# sigma = 0.03 plus four at each of four other magnitudes -- 28 defect-correction
# marches at 55-95 s each, about 21 minutes with the reproduction control -- and
# the twelve-window confirmation is four directions plus its control at 300-500 s
# an arm, about 40 minutes. The probe is 23 maps at ~90 s total. It reuses
# out/w202/*.npz, which are ignored and cost another 244 s at six windows and
# longer at twelve to rebuild.
!out/w205/
out/w205/*
!out/w205/w205.json

# a local clone of the poc1-windfarm-demo branch, for trying the bundle out
atlas-demo/
# Tier 49 (rung 9, the union marched: CS-18). JSON only: the record
# scripts/tier49_union_march.py writes -- the seven decisions with their
# controls (the clock table in seconds against the bare numbers L7/R9 compares,
# the rotor and machine sizing beside Tier 47's failure and the width-1 control,
# the body force's discrete-thrust identity, the multirate seams), the
# instrument run that fixed the gate, the seven arms and every clause's verdict,
# the slow half on its own clock, and W194's before/after compiles.
# tests/test_tier49_union_march.py asserts against it. The .npz caches hold the
# seven marches' traces and final fields -- about 4 MB, and rebuilding them is
# the five tight arms at 1200 macro-steps each, roughly 25-35 minutes in total
# on this host -- so they are ignored rather than committed.
!out/tier49/
out/tier49/*
!out/tier49/tier49.json
